caption: Rules of a Valid Hunt
setting-component: rules-of-a-valid-hunt

A sacrifice must be personal, individual, and ritualized. Current requirements are:

- The victim must be at least 25 years old and possess a higher soul.

- The hunter must act alone. A valid sacrifice is a solo hunt rather than a squad action.

- The hunter must personally inflict the killing injury.

- The killing weapon must be sanctified to Niktul.

- The weapon must be muscle-powered. Firearms and similar technological weapons do not qualify.

- The victim must die during the Blood Moon, before dawn.

- The death must be dedicated to Niktul and accepted by him as a sacrifice.

Appropriate weapons include knives, swords, axes, clubs, spears, bows, crossbows, thrown weapons, and similar muscle-powered arms. Edge cases such as poison, traps, indirect hazards, prior assistance, and the exact boundaries of “solo” remain to be formalized.

Niktul adjudicates whether a sacrifice genuinely satisfies the Covenant. Legal loopholes do not compel a god to accept a kill that violates the spirit of the Hunt.
